## Real-time gap encountered mid-session (factual note, not a defect)

The host clock jumped ~9.5 hours between tool calls during this session
(observed going from 2026-08-26T21:57 to 2026-08-27T07:19). A background
90s-spaced Playwright measurement run and a background jest run were both
killed by the interruption (confirmed via `ps aux` showing neither process
alive afterward, and the spaced-run log stopping mid-sequence after 3 of 4
planned sessions with no completion marker). The cached Supabase auth
token in scratchpad/auth.json also expired across the gap. Recorded here
because it explains why the next real-traffic measurement round (deploy ->
fresh auth token -> spaced Playwright sessions -> query
voice.latency.measured for nova_early_event) had not yet been re-run
before this VTID's PR was opened — that is the very next step once this
lands on staging.
